# Files Docker must NOT send to the build.
# Keeps secrets out of the image and keeps the build fast.
# Note: in this file a plain name only matches in the project root,
# so "**/" is used to match folders at any depth.

# --- Secrets: never put these inside an image ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# --- Git and editor files ---
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Python junk ---
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
venv
env
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.coverage
htmlcov

# --- Data and outputs (big, and not needed to run the app) ---
DATA
processed_data
evals
logs
*.log
.logfire
*.zip

# --- Docker files, docs and tools that do not belong inside an image ---
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
**/*.md
check_rules.py
requirements.txt